    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>,</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be the roots of the quadratic equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Then the area (in sq. units) bounded by the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> and the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> is",
